 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 20777,
   "ANSWER": "<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">A computer system is organized into several key components that work together to perform operations:</span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Central Processing Unit (CPU):</strong><br />\n\tThe brain of the system responsible for executing instructions. It contains:</span></span></span>\n\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU):</strong> Performs arithmetic and logical operations.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Control Unit (CU):</strong> Manages and coordinates all operations within the computer by interpreting instructions.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Registers:</strong> Small storage locations inside the CPU for holding data temporarily.</span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Memory Unit:</strong><br />\n\tStores data and instructions required for processing. It includes:</span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Primary Memory (RAM, ROM):</strong> Provides fast, volatile storage.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Cache Memory:</strong> Provides even faster access to frequently used data.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Secondary Memory (Hard Disk, SSD):</strong> Provides long-term data storage.</span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Input/Output Devices:</strong><br />\n\tAllow interaction with the computer system, e.g., keyboard, mouse, printers, and monitors.</span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list .5in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>System Bus:</strong><br />\n\tThe communication pathway that connects CPU, memory, and peripherals. Comprises:</span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Data Bus:</strong> Transfers data.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Address Bus:</strong> Carries memory addresses.</span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 1.0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Control Bus:</strong> Carries control signals.</span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">The coordination of these components allows the computer to execute tasks efficiently, with the system bus ensuring communication between them.</span></span></p>\n",
